--- body ---
## Problem

`erg check` emits a spurious warning in the source repo: `strayGoSource()` has a
self-exception checking for `module github.com/MinhHaDuong/git-erg` in go.mod,
but the actual module is `module git-erg`. The exception never fires → false positive.

Deeper issue: source code lived in `tickets/tools/go/` alongside the binary,
forcing a self-exception in the first place.

## Solution (structural)

Move Go source to `src/go/` and bootstrap binary to `tickets/erg`:
- `tickets/` holds only ticket files, support assets, and the binary
- `strayGoSource()` warns on any `.go`/`go.mod`/`go.sum` in the tickets dir,
  no exception needed — the source repo no longer has any there
- Legacy scan of `dir/tools/go/` kept for users who haven't migrated

Add `findTicketsDir()` for smart discovery: tries (1) directory containing the
binary (via manifest check), (2) `tickets/` under cwd, (3) cwd. Error with
informative message if none qualifies.

## Acceptance

- `erg check tickets/` in source repo emits 0 warnings.
- `./tickets/erg check` (no arg) discovers `tickets/` and passes.
- `make build` and `make test` green.
